bibliograph-web (0.2.16-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * 0.2.16 release: duration is an identifier claim.

    - The edition editor drops its edition-level `Duration (seconds)` input.
      Each identifier's `Shape` disclosure now carries a duration field beside
      Pages, so an abridged and an unabridged ISBN keep their own value, and
      the admin read model hashes the claim through the identifier bag instead
      of an edition column.
    - Edition saves and merges write
      `edition_identifier_info.duration_seconds` per identifier, and catalog
      reads take `durationSeconds` from `edition_identifier_shape`, so the
      published record and the XRPC edition view keep the field.
    - `durationSeconds` is no longer a merge field: duration travels with the
      identifier it belongs to.

