bibliograph-web (0.2.15-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * 0.2.15 release: edit shape claims and publisher links per identifier.

    - The edition editor drops the five edition-level shape inputs. Each
      identifier now carries a `Shape` disclosure with its own format, language,
      publication date, pages and description plus its publisher links (search
      an existing entity, create one by name, or remove). The Goodreads
      `Resolve from format` action moved onto the identifier row it answers for.
    - Saving diffs identifiers instead of replacing them, so untouched pairs
      keep their claims; an omitted `info`/`publishers` key leaves the stored
      rows alone, `null`/`[]` clears them, and unchanged claims are not
      rewritten (no `updated_at` bump, no needless republish).
    - Edition merges union publisher links per identifier pair (base first,
      positions renumbered) or apply the chosen source record's set to every
      identifier.
    - Catalog reads join `edition_identifier_shape`, and the completeness and
      identifier reports read the claim table and the publisher links.
    - Feed observability: the feed generator now exports
      `bibliograph_feed_request_duration_seconds`,
      `bibliograph_feed_page_items`, `bibliograph_feed_pages_total`,
      `bibliograph_feed_follow_dids`, `bibliograph_feed_query_duration_seconds`
      and `bibliograph_feed_auth_failures_total`, the last labelled by a bounded
      reason (`missing`, `format`, `claims`, `expired`, `issuer`, `signature`)
      carried on `FeedAuthError.reason`, so rejections are countable without
      parsing messages.

