bibliograph-web (0.2.13-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * 0.2.13 release: merge one contributor into another.

    - New `/admin/contributor/<id>/merge` page, reachable from the contributor
      editor's heading and prefilled by `?into=<id|at-uri>`: it searches the
      same local typeahead, previews what the merge will do, and confirms
      through a form action. `packages/web/src/lib/server/admin/entity-merge.ts`
      does the write in one transaction: the survivor keeps its id, at-URI,
      name and creation date; blank fields (description, inverted name, image
      URL, born, died) and unused identifiers are absorbed, keeping the
      survivor's pair but filling in a provider `url` it lacks; every edition
      credit is repointed at the survivor, except one whose normalized role the
      survivor already holds there, which is dropped; an edge `ref` naming the
      absorbed row's at-URI is cleared; the absorbed row is deleted last and its
      record delete is queued. Publication stays trigger-driven.
    - Both rows must still carry the revisions the page loaded (409
      `EntityChanged`); the same row on both sides is 400, an unknown ref 404,
      and absorbing identifiers that already belong to a third row is 409
      `DuplicateEntity` with both rows untouched.
    - No XRPC surface change: the described method count is unchanged.

